  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the Early 19th-Century Trieu To Temple Front Building at Hu Imperial City</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Built in the early 19th century as part of the imperial city at Hu, Trieu To Temple is one of a handful of remaining buildings from the early years of the Nguyen dynasty, Vietnams last dynasty but the first to unify the country. This project addresses the conservation needs of the bipartite temples front building.</narrative>
  </description>
